/-!
# `ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L)` into the section ring of `L = φ⁎𝒪_{U_d}(d)`

Let `S` be a graded ring, `X = Proj(S)`, `d ≥ 1`, `U_d = ⋃_{f ∈ S_d} D₊(f)` the open of Equation
27.12.0.1 and `φ : Y ⟶ U_d` a morphism of schemes. Put `L = φ⁎𝒪_{U_d}(d)`. Stacks Equation
27.12.0.3 (Tag 01N7) composes the graded ring map `ψ^d : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(U_d, 𝒪_{U_d}(d))` of the
universal family (Tag 01N6) with pullback along `φ`, to get a graded ring map

`ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L) = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(Y, L^{⊗ n})`,

and observes that `L` is invertible and generated by the global sections `ψ^d_φ(f)`, `f ∈ S_d`.
This file states and proves exactly that, with `Γ_*(Y, L)` the section ring of Tag 01CV,
`Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing L`, graded by its summands and multiplied by the tensor-power
multiplication `Stacks.GradedSections.mul`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.pullbackUniversalTwist`: the invertible module
  `L = φ⁎𝒪_{U_d}(d)` on `Y`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackPowSections`: the degreewise maps
  `S_{nd} ⟶ Γ(Y, L^{⊗ n})` of `ψ^d_φ`, multiplicative across degrees.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSectionRing`: **the graded ring
  homomorphism `ψ^d_φ : S^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L)`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSectionRing_apply_homogeneous`: on a
  homogeneous element `a` of Veronese degree `n`, `ψ^d_φ(a)` is the pullback along `φ` of the
  global section of `𝒪_{U_d}(d)^{⊗ n}` that the section of `𝒪_{U_d}(nd)` attached to `a` defines
  through `θ : 𝒪_{U_d}(d)^{⊗ n} ≅ 𝒪_{U_d}(nd)`, placed in the degree `n` summand.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.generatesStalks_psiPullbackPowSections`: `L` is
  generated by the sections `ψ^d_φ(f)`, `f ∈ S_d`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSectionRing_spec`: **Tag 01N7**, the three
  assertions together.

## Implementation notes

The two halves of multiplicativity are imported. On `U_d` it is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOpenUniversalTriple.universalVeroneseSections`, whose
multiplicativity is the multiplicativity of `θ` (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.thetaNat_mul`)
read on the sections attached to homogeneous elements; along `φ` it is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartPullbackCotensorator.pullSection_mulSections`, the compatibility
of pullback with the multiplication of tensor powers. Both are stated for the product
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.mulSections` on honest global sections, and
`secOf_mulSections` below carries that to the product of the section ring. The unit axiom is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTripleUnitSection.toFun_zero_eq_unitGlobal`, which derives it from
generation in degree one.

The older `psiPullback_gradedRingHom_and_generatesStalks` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProjGradedRing` is the twist-model form: its target
has degree `n` piece `Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(nd))` rather than `Γ(Y, L^{⊗ n})`.

The commutative ring structure on `Γ_*(Y, L)` is the direct sum's own, built from
`Stacks.GradedSections.instGRing`; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.Basic` for why
`Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeSectionCommRing` is not installed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Equation 01N7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

